 },
 "notes": "mul multiplies albedo, rough multiplies roughness, snow is coverage on up-facing surfaces, tint/tintAmt lean the albedo, autumn picks one colour per instance or material, leafless hides *_leaves nodes, puddles shows *_puddles nodes. pond is standing water on flat ground (0..1, how much of it), moss is growth on up and north faces, dew is sheen and glints. light.snowDepth is metres of lying snow once fully accumulated; accumulate gives seconds to build, melt, fill and drain. ice is the glaze a role takes in freezing rain (black ice on asphalt); freezing keeps lying snow from melting and lets ice build. biomes.<map> overrides roles and light for that map (shield = Pike Narrows, desert = Ochre Basin)."
